WEBVTT

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:01.936
Cambridge English Readers.

00:00:01.996 --> 00:00:03.299
Level 1.

00:00:03.359 --> 00:00:24.850
Next Door to Love by Margaret Johnson.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:01:01.136
Next Door to Love by Margaret Johnson Chapter 1 The Man at Number 3 My friend Janet looked out of my living room window.

00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:03.037
Who is that?

00:01:03.097 --> 00:01:04.528
She asked.

00:01:04.588 --> 00:01:09.480
I went to look He lives here, I said.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.244
He lives here in Bridge Street, Janet asked.

00:01:14.304 --> 00:01:16.446
Yes, I said.

00:01:16.506 --> 00:01:21.670
At number three, next door to me, he's my new neighbor.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.962
Janet smiled.

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:27.416
He's very tall, she said.

00:01:27.476 --> 00:01:30.128
And I like his black hair.

00:01:30.188 --> 00:01:35.328
Janet, I said, come away from the window.

00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:38.574
I didn't want my new neighbor to see us.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.505
She turned to me.

00:01:40.565 --> 00:01:43.316
It's okay, she said.

00:01:43.376 --> 00:01:44.907
I'm just looking.

00:01:44.927 --> 00:01:47.678
I don't want a new man.

00:01:47.738 --> 00:01:49.729
I've got David.

00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:52.730
David is Janet's boyfriend.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:56.542
I'm only thinking of you, she said.

00:01:56.602 --> 00:01:59.604
You need a new boyfriend.

00:01:59.664 --> 00:02:02.095
What's your neighbor's job?

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:03.711
She asked me.

00:02:03.771 --> 00:02:06.798
I don't know," I said.

00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:09.368
Well, how old is he?

00:02:09.388 --> 00:02:11.959
I looked at her.

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:15.770
I don't know Janet, I said.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.640
Has he got a girlfriend?

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.511
Janet, I said.

00:02:21.571 --> 00:02:24.212
I don't know anything about him.

00:02:24.232 --> 00:02:28.733
I saw him yesterday and we said hello.

00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:30.221
That's all.

00:02:30.281 --> 00:02:35.130
Janet always wanted me to go out and meet new men.

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:39.842
You need to go out, Stella, she often told me.

00:02:39.902 --> 00:02:44.444
You need to meet new people, new men.

00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:48.086
But I didn't want to meet new men.

00:02:48.146 --> 00:02:50.736
And I didn't want a boyfriend.

00:02:50.796 --> 00:02:55.109
I knew boyfriends didn't always make you happy.

00:02:55.168 --> 00:03:00.041
My last boyfriend, James, didn't make me happy.

00:03:00.101 --> 00:03:02.574
Janet looked at me.

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:06.446
You're thinking about James, she said.

00:03:06.506 --> 00:03:09.748
Janet often knows what I'm thinking.

00:03:09.808 --> 00:03:13.402
Don't think about him, she said.

00:03:13.462 --> 00:03:16.444
He wasn't any good for you.

00:03:16.504 --> 00:03:20.036
But you mustn't think all men are bad.

00:03:20.096 --> 00:03:22.978
Your neighbour looks nice.

00:03:23.038 --> 00:03:29.337
Stop talking about him, I told her, and we laughed.

00:03:29.397 --> 00:03:37.346
Janet left my house at about six o'clock and I went up to change for my tennis class.

00:03:37.406 --> 00:03:40.538
My neighbour was out in his garden.

00:03:40.598 --> 00:03:45.642
It was August and there were lots of flowers in all the gardens.

00:03:45.702 --> 00:03:52.496
The flowers in the garden at number three were yellow, red, orange and pink.

00:03:52.556 --> 00:03:54.448
Happy colours.

00:03:54.508 --> 00:03:58.578
But my neighbour didn't look happy.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:03.460
You're sad, I thought, as I looked down at him.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.122
Why?

00:04:05.182 --> 00:04:07.814
Why are you sad?

00:04:07.874 --> 00:04:13.720
Then he looked up, and I came away from the window quickly.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.254
I saw my neighbour again the next morning in the street.

00:04:18.314 --> 00:04:20.326
He looked tired.

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:22.708
Hello, I said.

00:04:22.768 --> 00:04:25.645
It's a beautiful day.

00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:28.422
Yes, he said.

00:04:28.482 --> 00:04:30.024
It's hot again.

00:04:30.084 --> 00:04:31.956
Too hot for work.

00:04:32.016 --> 00:04:34.598
Then he smiled at me.

00:04:34.658 --> 00:04:37.702
My name's Tony, he said.

00:04:37.762 --> 00:04:39.683
Tony Bryant.

00:04:39.743 --> 00:04:41.645
I took his hand.

00:04:41.705 --> 00:04:44.348
Hello, Tony, I said.

00:04:44.407 --> 00:04:47.801
I'm Stella, Stella Greenwood.

00:04:47.861 --> 00:04:51.596
Good to meet you, Stella, he said.

00:04:51.656 --> 00:04:57.089
I didn't see Tony the next day, all the day after that.

00:04:57.149 --> 00:05:02.870
Then, on the Friday morning, I heard him on the phone next door.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:09.041
The houses in Bridge Street are small, and you can sometimes hear people speaking.

00:05:09.101 --> 00:05:14.132
And I heard everything that Tony Bryant said that morning.

00:05:14.192 --> 00:05:16.422
He was very angry.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:20.516
You can't do this, Kathy, he said.

00:05:20.576 --> 00:05:23.121
You can't do this to me again.

00:05:23.141 --> 00:05:25.804
I want to see her.

00:05:25.864 --> 00:05:29.586
Please, Cathy, don't do this."

00:05:29.645 --> 00:05:33.908
I sat at my breakfast table and listened.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.380
Cathy?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.770
Cathy?

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.072
Oh!

00:05:38.131 --> 00:05:43.306
I heard Tony say, and then he put the phone down.

00:05:43.366 --> 00:05:47.818
I ate an apple and thought about Tony Bryant.

00:05:47.878 --> 00:05:50.120
Who was Cathy?

00:05:50.179 --> 00:05:52.882
And what was Tony afraid of?

00:05:52.942 --> 00:05:56.715
Because I knew he was afraid of something.

00:05:56.775 --> 00:06:00.868
There's something Janet always says to me.

00:06:00.928 --> 00:06:04.011
Something that's very important to her.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:09.395
She says, when you want to do something, just do it.

00:06:09.455 --> 00:06:11.967
Don't stop and think about it.

00:06:12.027 --> 00:06:13.198
Don't wait.

00:06:13.258 --> 00:06:14.814
Just do it.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:19.950
And that's what I did, after I heard Tony Bryant on the phone.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:27.272
I didn't stop and think I put my apple down on the table and went to the house next door.

00:06:27.332 --> 00:06:29.983
I had to wait a long time.

00:06:30.043 --> 00:06:32.764
Then Tony answered the door.

00:06:32.824 --> 00:06:35.375
Yes, he said.

00:06:35.435 --> 00:06:37.776
He didn't look very happy.

00:06:37.836 --> 00:06:42.297
And then, of course, I didn't know what to say.

00:06:42.357 --> 00:06:45.493
Yes, he said again.

00:06:45.553 --> 00:06:48.009
What do you want, Stella?

00:06:48.069 --> 00:06:52.892
I started to blush, then, and my face felt hot.

00:06:52.952 --> 00:06:54.002
I...

00:06:54.062 --> 00:06:55.362
I wanted...

00:06:55.422 --> 00:06:56.933
I started to say...

00:06:56.953 --> 00:07:00.585
I just wanted to know...

00:07:00.645 --> 00:07:02.796
And I stopped.

00:07:02.856 --> 00:07:05.538
You wanted to know what?

00:07:05.597 --> 00:07:07.333
Tony said.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:10.828
Well, are you all right?

00:07:10.888 --> 00:07:13.819
I asked, and he looked at me.

00:07:13.879 --> 00:07:21.591
His face was cold, but I thought he was just sad or angry about something.

00:07:21.651 --> 00:07:25.122
Yes, thank you, he said.

00:07:25.182 --> 00:07:27.062
I'm all right.

00:07:27.122 --> 00:07:29.452
I blushed some more.

00:07:29.512 --> 00:07:32.023
Oh, I said.

00:07:32.083 --> 00:07:34.734
Okay, good.

00:07:34.794 --> 00:07:36.294
That's good.

00:07:36.354 --> 00:07:37.516
Good.

00:07:37.576 --> 00:07:43.090
Well, by then, and I left quickly.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.522
But then Tony called after me.

00:07:46.582 --> 00:07:49.084
Steller, wait.

00:07:49.144 --> 00:07:52.926
I stopped and looked back at him.

00:07:52.986 --> 00:07:56.698
I'm sorry, he said.

00:07:56.758 --> 00:07:59.640
It was nice of you to ask.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:03.032
Have you got time to come in for a coffee?

00:08:03.092 --> 00:08:05.233
I looked at my watch.

00:08:05.293 --> 00:08:07.527
It was nine o'clock.

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:10.261
Not now, I said.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.962
Sorry, Tony.

00:08:12.022 --> 00:08:14.044
I'm late for work.

00:08:14.104 --> 00:08:16.566
Okay, he said.

00:08:16.626 --> 00:08:21.718
I'm going away today, but come for coffee next weekend.

00:08:21.778 --> 00:08:23.960
I smiled at him.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:28.524
Thank you, I said.

00:08:28.584 --> 00:08:43.500
Chapter 2 Flowers from Daisy The next weekend, it was hot again, and I wanted to sit in the sun all day.

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:48.082
I took a book and a drink, and went out into the garden.

00:08:48.142 --> 00:08:51.713
And that's when I heard the child.

00:08:51.773 --> 00:08:55.994
I'm going out, the child said.

00:08:56.054 --> 00:09:02.717
And then a small face looked at me from Tony's garden, a little girl's face.

00:09:02.777 --> 00:09:06.352
Hello, the little girl said to me.

00:09:06.412 --> 00:09:10.560
She had lots of black hair under her big sun hat.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.280
Hello, I said.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.202
Who are you?

00:09:15.262 --> 00:09:18.074
Daisy, she said.

00:09:18.134 --> 00:09:20.114
That's a flower.

00:09:20.174 --> 00:09:22.086
I like flowers.

00:09:22.146 --> 00:09:24.478
Do you like flowers?

00:09:24.538 --> 00:09:26.908
I smile better.

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:32.590
She was about five or six years old, but who was she?

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:34.638
Then Tony came out.

00:09:34.698 --> 00:09:39.740
He stood next to Daisy, and I knew who she was.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:43.100
Hello, he said to me.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.801
This is my daughter, Daisy.

00:09:45.821 --> 00:09:49.272
Hello, Daisy, I said.

00:09:49.332 --> 00:09:52.224
And I saw that Tony was happy.

00:09:52.284 --> 00:09:54.614
Very happy.

00:09:54.674 --> 00:09:58.055
Can she come to tea with us, Daddy?

00:09:58.115 --> 00:10:00.660
Daisy asked her father.

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.107
She has a name," Tony told her.

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:07.328
She's called Stella.

00:10:07.388 --> 00:10:11.310
Okay, can Stella come to tea with us?

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.921
Daisy asked.

00:10:12.981 --> 00:10:15.332
Tony smiled at me.

00:10:15.392 --> 00:10:18.704
Of course she can, he said.

00:10:18.764 --> 00:10:24.387
We sat in Tony's garden, and Daisy told me all about her cat.

00:10:24.447 --> 00:10:26.738
She talked a lot.

00:10:26.798 --> 00:10:29.978
He's black and white, she said.

00:10:30.038 --> 00:10:31.728
Like a cow.

00:10:31.788 --> 00:10:36.209
I call him Moo Moo, like the noise cows make.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.140
But he drinks milk.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.740
Cows don't drink milk.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.082
Cows make milk, Tony told her.

00:10:45.142 --> 00:10:48.163
He smiled at me over Daisy's head.

00:10:48.223 --> 00:10:50.513
Daisy looked at him.

00:10:50.573 --> 00:10:54.024
I know that, Daddy, she said.

00:10:54.084 --> 00:10:57.178
I'm not a little girl anymore.

00:10:57.238 --> 00:11:00.193
And she went to look at the flowers.

00:11:00.253 --> 00:11:04.094
She's lovely, I told Tony.

00:11:04.154 --> 00:11:07.726
He looked at his daughter and smiled.

00:11:07.786 --> 00:11:10.077
Yes, he said.

00:11:10.137 --> 00:11:11.728
She is.

00:11:11.788 --> 00:11:14.569
Then he looked sad.

00:11:14.629 --> 00:11:20.642
But I don't see her very often, because her mother and I aren't together now.

00:11:20.702 --> 00:11:25.040
That's why he's sad, I thought.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.088
I'm sorry Tony, I said.

00:11:29.148 --> 00:11:33.600
I'm okay now, Tony said quickly.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:36.080
He smiled at me.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.981
Anyway, how are you?

00:11:39.041 --> 00:11:40.931
How is your week?

00:11:40.991 --> 00:11:43.592
It was good, I said.

00:11:43.652 --> 00:11:46.282
There was a lot to do at work.

00:11:46.342 --> 00:11:48.633
Tony smiled.

00:11:48.693 --> 00:11:51.003
What do you do?

00:11:51.063 --> 00:11:55.657
I'm one of the cooks at Marcello's Italian restaurant.

00:11:55.717 --> 00:11:58.942
You're a chef, he said.

00:11:59.002 --> 00:12:01.153
That's a good job.

00:12:01.213 --> 00:12:04.626
Yes, I said, I love it.

00:12:04.686 --> 00:12:06.416
What about you?

00:12:06.476 --> 00:12:07.687
What do you do?

00:12:07.707 --> 00:12:12.230
I work with computers, Tony told me.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.692
Daisy came over to us again.

00:12:14.712 --> 00:12:20.614
These are for you, she said, and she gave us some flowers.

00:12:20.674 --> 00:12:24.035
Thank you, Daisy," we said.

00:12:24.095 --> 00:12:29.118
She smiled at us, and then ran away across the garden.

00:12:29.178 --> 00:12:33.239
Leave some flowers in the garden, please, Daisy.

00:12:33.299 --> 00:12:34.930
Tony told her.

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:36.951
They looked nice there.

00:12:37.011 --> 00:12:40.972
I put my face into the red and orange flowers.

00:12:41.032 --> 00:12:43.494
They were beautiful.

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:47.346
I think she likes you, Tony told me.

00:12:47.406 --> 00:12:49.206
I smiled at him.

00:12:49.266 --> 00:12:51.365
I like her, too.

00:12:51.425 --> 00:12:55.326
Tony looked at the flowers in his hand.

00:12:55.386 --> 00:13:01.090
Some of me dies when Daisy's away from me, he said.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:03.422
Then he looked at me.

00:13:03.482 --> 00:13:09.148
Daisy lives with her mother, Cathy, and Cathy's husband, Cameron.

00:13:09.208 --> 00:13:11.439
Tony looked away.

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:16.203
Daisy's got a new family now, he said.

00:13:16.263 --> 00:13:18.976
Well, now I knew.

00:13:19.036 --> 00:13:24.221
Kathy, the woman on the phone, was Daisy's mother.

00:13:24.281 --> 00:13:27.314
That's sad, I said.

00:13:27.374 --> 00:13:29.215
Tony smiled.

00:13:29.275 --> 00:13:31.186
But he wasn't happy.

00:13:31.246 --> 00:13:32.488
Yes.

00:13:32.548 --> 00:13:35.420
Oh, I know Daisy likes Cameron.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.562
But he isn't her father.

00:13:37.622 --> 00:13:39.283
I am.

00:13:39.343 --> 00:13:42.166
How often do you see Daisy?

00:13:42.226 --> 00:13:43.736
I asked.

00:13:43.796 --> 00:13:45.808
Not very often.

00:13:45.868 --> 00:13:48.914
But she sees Cameron every day.

00:13:48.974 --> 00:13:53.279
Anyway, she's here today, Tony said.

00:13:53.339 --> 00:13:55.030
And I'm happy.

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:58.552
Daisy looked over and smiled at us.

00:13:58.612 --> 00:14:01.452
I smiled back at her.

00:14:01.512 --> 00:14:06.205
I can understand computers, Tony told me.

00:14:06.265 --> 00:14:12.998
I know what they're going to do, but I don't always understand people.

00:14:13.058 --> 00:14:17.620
I thought about James and all his girlfriends.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.069
No.

00:14:19.129 --> 00:14:24.121
We don't always know what people are going to do, I said.

00:14:24.181 --> 00:14:28.502
Next day, I met up with Janet in town.

00:14:28.562 --> 00:14:31.083
We went to a cafe for a drink.

00:14:31.143 --> 00:14:37.125
She asked about Tony, and I told her about my afternoon with him.

00:14:37.185 --> 00:14:40.406
Did he ask you to go out with him?

00:14:40.466 --> 00:14:42.166
She wanted to know.

00:14:42.226 --> 00:14:44.547
No, I said.

00:14:44.607 --> 00:14:47.058
He's just my neighbour.

00:14:47.118 --> 00:14:50.250
But I blushed, and Janet saw.

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:53.552
You like him, she told me.

00:14:53.612 --> 00:14:56.483
Yes, all right, I said.

00:14:56.544 --> 00:14:58.654
I do like him.

00:14:58.714 --> 00:15:01.816
But he's a very sad man.

00:15:01.877 --> 00:15:06.308
I think he's still in love with Daisy's mother, Cathy.

00:15:06.368 --> 00:15:08.850
Janet looked at me.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:12.942
But you said Cathy is Cameron's wife now.

00:15:13.002 --> 00:15:15.054
Yes, I said.

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:17.586
Cathy is Cameron's wife.

00:15:17.646 --> 00:15:21.718
But Tony still thinks about the time when they were a family.

00:15:21.778 --> 00:15:24.600
Him, Daisy and Cathy.

00:15:24.661 --> 00:15:29.354
I don't think he understands why everything changed.

00:15:29.414 --> 00:15:32.996
That is sad, Janet said.

00:15:33.056 --> 00:15:35.077
Then she looked at me.

00:15:35.137 --> 00:15:40.070
Well, she said, you need a man to laugh with.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:43.316
So I don't think Tony is good for you.

00:15:43.376 --> 00:15:46.371
I don't need a man, Janet.

00:15:46.431 --> 00:15:47.682
I told her.

00:15:47.742 --> 00:15:50.624
I'm happy without a boyfriend.

00:15:50.684 --> 00:15:52.934
But Janet looked at me.

00:15:52.994 --> 00:15:56.196
Everybody needs someone, Stella.

00:15:56.256 --> 00:15:59.628
She said.

00:15:59.688 --> 00:16:03.670
Chapter 3.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.130
Everybody needs someone.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:15.322
The next day, lots of people came to Marcello's restaurant, and I had lots of food to cook.

00:16:15.382 --> 00:16:22.158
The weather was still warm, and in the kitchen it was very, very hot.

00:16:22.218 --> 00:16:25.200
I was happy to have lots to do.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.762
I didn't want to think about Janet's words.

00:16:28.822 --> 00:16:32.564
Everybody needs someone, Stella.

00:16:32.624 --> 00:16:36.507
But of course, I did think about them.

00:16:36.567 --> 00:16:38.267
All day.

00:16:38.326 --> 00:16:43.597
I also thought about James, and how he made me sad.

00:16:43.657 --> 00:16:51.080
Then I thought about Tony, and how Kathy made him sad, and then Daisy.

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:53.792
They all enjoyed their food.

00:16:53.852 --> 00:16:57.474
Klaus, one of the waiters, told me in the afternoon.

00:16:57.534 --> 00:16:59.374
I liked Klaus.

00:16:59.435 --> 00:17:05.207
He was over in England, from Germany for six months, and he was always happy.

00:17:05.267 --> 00:17:07.693
Good, I replied.

00:17:07.753 --> 00:17:11.470
Do you want to go out with me tonight, Stella?"

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.291
Klaus asked me.

00:17:13.351 --> 00:17:15.482
I'm going to the cinema.

00:17:15.542 --> 00:17:17.233
Can you come?

00:17:17.293 --> 00:17:20.454
I thought about Janet's words again.

00:17:20.514 --> 00:17:23.906
Everybody needs someone, Stella.

00:17:23.966 --> 00:17:27.488
Then I looked at Klaus and smiled.

00:17:27.549 --> 00:17:30.290
Yes, okay, I said.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:36.229
When I got home at six o'clock, Tony was taking things out of his car.

00:17:36.289 --> 00:17:39.066
Hi, Stella," he said.

00:17:39.126 --> 00:17:40.978
I smiled at him.

00:17:41.038 --> 00:17:45.380
He looked good in his black work trousers and white shirt.

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:46.921
Hi, Tony.

00:17:46.981 --> 00:17:48.242
How are you?

00:17:48.302 --> 00:17:51.614
Very well, thank you, he replied.

00:17:51.674 --> 00:17:53.715
It's good to see you.

00:17:53.775 --> 00:17:55.996
Yes, I said.

00:17:56.056 --> 00:17:58.358
It's good to see you too.

00:17:58.418 --> 00:18:02.010
I'm going out for a drink tonight, he said.

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.221
At the treehouse bar.

00:18:04.281 --> 00:18:06.378
He looked at me.

00:18:06.438 --> 00:18:09.415
Do you want to come with me, Stella?"

00:18:09.475 --> 00:18:11.958
I stopped smiling.

00:18:12.018 --> 00:18:13.259
Oh!

00:18:13.319 --> 00:18:14.620
I replied.

00:18:14.680 --> 00:18:16.042
I can't.

00:18:16.102 --> 00:18:17.854
I'm sorry, Tony.

00:18:17.914 --> 00:18:20.436
I'm going to the cinema tonight.

00:18:20.496 --> 00:18:25.751
That's okay, Tony said, and he walked to his house.

00:18:25.811 --> 00:18:30.262
I looked at Tony's back as he opened his front door.

00:18:30.322 --> 00:18:34.360
I didn't want to go to the cinema with Klaus now.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:38.132
I wanted to go out for a drink with Tony.

00:18:38.192 --> 00:18:40.952
How about tomorrow night?

00:18:41.012 --> 00:18:42.373
I asked.

00:18:42.433 --> 00:18:46.865
Tony looked back at me and smiled.

00:18:46.925 --> 00:18:49.756
Okay, he said.

00:18:49.816 --> 00:18:51.287
Good.

00:18:51.347 --> 00:18:53.358
Eight o'clock then?

00:18:53.418 --> 00:18:55.508
I smiled at him.

00:18:55.568 --> 00:18:59.402
Eight o'clock tomorrow, I replied.

00:18:59.462 --> 00:19:02.626
I enjoyed going out with Klaus.

00:19:02.686 --> 00:19:06.418
The film was called Dead Men Can't Speak.

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:09.300
It was a very bad film.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.041
But it made me and Klaus laugh.

00:19:12.101 --> 00:19:14.712
I need a drink after that.

00:19:14.772 --> 00:19:17.193
Klaus set when we came out.

00:19:17.254 --> 00:19:20.465
And we went to a bar near the cinema.

00:19:20.525 --> 00:19:23.706
Sorry about the film, Stella.

00:19:23.766 --> 00:19:26.294
He said when we had our drinks.

00:19:26.355 --> 00:19:31.264
Next time, we can go to a film you want to see.

00:19:31.325 --> 00:19:34.816
But I just smiled and drank my drink.

00:19:34.876 --> 00:19:41.402
I liked Klaus, but I didn't want to think about next time now.

00:19:41.462 --> 00:19:45.744
After the bar, Klaus walked home with me.

00:19:45.804 --> 00:19:51.719
I knew he wanted me to ask him into the house, but I didn't.

00:19:51.779 --> 00:19:55.740
Thank you for tonight, Klaus, I said.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.508
I enjoyed it.

00:19:57.568 --> 00:20:00.540
See you tomorrow would work."

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:05.834
I think he was a little sad, but he smiled anyway.

00:20:05.894 --> 00:20:08.806
Okay, Stella, he said.

00:20:08.866 --> 00:20:10.868
See you tomorrow.

00:20:10.928 --> 00:20:13.208
I opened my front door.

00:20:13.269 --> 00:20:18.392
Stella, Klaus said behind me, and I looked at him.

00:20:18.452 --> 00:20:19.904
Yes?

00:20:19.964 --> 00:20:22.886
I like you a lot.

00:20:22.946 --> 00:20:25.494
Thank you, I said.

00:20:25.554 --> 00:20:27.080
Good night.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:31.321
Then I went into my house and closed the door.

00:20:31.381 --> 00:20:35.712
I didn't say, I like you too, Klaus.

00:20:35.772 --> 00:20:38.562
Because I didn't know what I thought.

00:20:38.622 --> 00:20:40.442
I liked him.

00:20:40.502 --> 00:20:47.934
But did I want to be his girlfriend or just his friend?

00:20:47.994 --> 00:20:51.915
Chapter four.

00:20:51.975 --> 00:20:54.560
Drinks for two.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:21:03.160
When I got home from work the next evening, I washed my hair and put on a new dress.

00:21:03.221 --> 00:21:08.744
You look nice, Tony told me, when we met at eight o'clock.

00:21:08.804 --> 00:21:11.275
Thank you, I said.

00:21:11.335 --> 00:21:15.567
Tony's blue shard was like the blue of his eyes.

00:21:15.628 --> 00:21:18.309
He looked good too.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:20.420
Bring your jacket.

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:23.548
Then we can sit out, he said.

00:21:23.608 --> 00:21:27.267
I got a jacket, and then we left.

00:21:27.327 --> 00:21:29.989
I love warm evenings.

00:21:30.049 --> 00:21:33.081
Tony said as we walked down the street.

00:21:33.141 --> 00:21:37.284
When I first met Cathy, we lived in Scotland.

00:21:37.344 --> 00:21:41.416
It gets dark at 11 o'clock there at this time of year.

00:21:41.476 --> 00:21:44.248
I loved the long evenings.

00:21:44.308 --> 00:21:48.682
I didn't say anything, and he looked at me.

00:21:48.742 --> 00:21:51.467
Sorry, he said.

00:21:51.527 --> 00:21:54.972
I know I talk about the old days a lot.

00:21:55.032 --> 00:21:57.693
That's okay, I said.

00:21:57.753 --> 00:22:00.004
No, he said.

00:22:00.064 --> 00:22:02.015
It isn't okay.

00:22:02.075 --> 00:22:05.406
I don't want to think about the old days tonight.

00:22:05.466 --> 00:22:08.528
I just want to think about now.

00:22:08.588 --> 00:22:11.118
I was happy to hear that.

00:22:11.178 --> 00:22:16.210
And when I smiled at him, he smiled back.

00:22:16.270 --> 00:22:21.983
I want to know everything about you, Stella, he told me.

00:22:22.043 --> 00:22:25.006
Everything, I asked.

00:22:25.066 --> 00:22:27.537
Yes, he said.

00:22:27.597 --> 00:22:29.548
Everything.

00:22:29.608 --> 00:22:34.030
There were lots of people in the garden at the treehouse bar.

00:22:34.090 --> 00:22:39.064
Men and women sitting at small tables having conversations.

00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:40.594
Couples.

00:22:40.654 --> 00:22:46.128
And when Tony and I sat at a table, we were a couple too.

00:22:46.188 --> 00:22:48.409
I like it here.

00:22:48.469 --> 00:22:50.060
Tony said.

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:52.622
Yes, I said.

00:22:52.682 --> 00:22:54.822
I do, too.

00:22:54.882 --> 00:22:58.034
Tony had his drink in his hand.

00:22:58.094 --> 00:23:00.224
He smiled at me.

00:23:00.284 --> 00:23:04.366
He is to good neighbors, he said.

00:23:04.426 --> 00:23:06.937
To good neighbors.

00:23:06.997 --> 00:23:10.318
Then Tony looked at me.

00:23:10.378 --> 00:23:14.640
Tell me about your job, he said.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:17.891
What food do you like to cook?

00:23:17.951 --> 00:23:20.654
I thought about it.

00:23:20.714 --> 00:23:24.908
food with lots of color," I said.

00:23:24.968 --> 00:23:28.110
I like my meals to look good.

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:30.872
That's very important to me.

00:23:30.932 --> 00:23:35.524
I must come and eat at your restaurant, Tony said.

00:23:35.584 --> 00:23:38.976
I spoke quickly without thinking.

00:23:39.036 --> 00:23:42.918
Or I can cook for you at home, I said.

00:23:42.979 --> 00:23:45.370
Tony smiled.

00:23:45.430 --> 00:23:48.761
Yes, please, he said.

00:23:48.822 --> 00:23:50.908
I love my job.

00:23:50.968 --> 00:23:52.604
I told him.

00:23:52.664 --> 00:23:57.174
When I was a child, I cooked with my mother.

00:23:57.234 --> 00:24:00.265
Daisy likes to cook with her mother.

00:24:00.325 --> 00:24:01.986
Tony told me.

00:24:02.046 --> 00:24:04.646
His face went sad.

00:24:04.706 --> 00:24:06.727
They make cakes.

00:24:06.787 --> 00:24:09.688
Kathy's a good cook too.

00:24:09.748 --> 00:24:11.758
I looked at him.

00:24:11.818 --> 00:24:13.949
What does Kathy do?

00:24:14.009 --> 00:24:15.489
I asked.

00:24:15.549 --> 00:24:17.390
She's a teacher.

00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:19.128
He told me.

00:24:19.188 --> 00:24:22.748
But I don't want to talk about Cathy.

00:24:22.808 --> 00:24:26.960
Tell me about you, your family.

00:24:27.020 --> 00:24:29.182
Where do they live?

00:24:29.242 --> 00:24:40.016
I told him and he listened, but I felt there were three people at the table now, me, Toni and Cathy.

00:24:40.076 --> 00:24:45.278
I stopped talking about my family and looked at him.

00:24:45.338 --> 00:24:49.680
Tell me about you and Cathy, I said.

00:24:49.740 --> 00:24:53.052
Tony looked down at his drink.

00:24:53.112 --> 00:24:55.584
Kathy left me.

00:24:55.644 --> 00:24:59.568
She met Cameron at work, he said.

00:24:59.628 --> 00:25:02.880
She left me because she wanted to be with him.

00:25:02.901 --> 00:25:08.806
I loved someone too, I told him.

00:25:08.866 --> 00:25:14.810
James, but he had lots of girlfriends.

00:25:14.870 --> 00:25:19.133
Tony put his hand on mine.

00:25:19.193 --> 00:25:22.834
Do you want to meet someone new?"

00:25:22.894 --> 00:25:24.856
he asked.

00:25:24.916 --> 00:25:28.328
I don't know, I said.

00:25:28.388 --> 00:25:30.350
I'm afraid.

00:25:30.410 --> 00:25:32.802
He smiled at me.

00:25:32.862 --> 00:25:37.726
Well, I'm also afraid, he said.

00:25:37.786 --> 00:25:40.758
But I do like you, Stella.

00:25:40.818 --> 00:25:43.460
I like you a lot.

00:25:43.520 --> 00:25:47.705
And I like you, Tony, I said.

00:25:47.765 --> 00:25:52.880
As I looked at him, I knew how I felt about Klaus.

00:25:52.940 --> 00:25:55.251
Klaus and I were friends.

00:25:55.311 --> 00:25:56.792
That was all.

00:25:56.852 --> 00:26:00.764
I liked him, and I laughed with him.

00:26:00.824 --> 00:26:07.158
But when Klaus looked at me, I didn't feel like this.

00:26:07.218 --> 00:26:10.800
Tony looked into my eyes.

00:26:10.860 --> 00:26:13.758
Good, he said.

00:26:13.818 --> 00:26:16.685
Then come to tea at the weekend.

00:26:16.745 --> 00:26:20.156
Daisy told me she wants to see you again.

00:26:20.216 --> 00:26:23.988
And I want to see you again too.

00:26:24.048 --> 00:26:27.619
I went to tea with them on Sunday.

00:26:27.679 --> 00:26:31.170
We played football and got very hot.

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:37.942
Then, when Daisy was in bed, Tony and I went into the garden.

00:26:38.002 --> 00:26:43.051
We sat and talked, and Tony took my hand in his.

00:26:43.111 --> 00:26:46.000
And then I looked up at him.

00:26:46.060 --> 00:26:48.662
And he kissed me.

00:26:48.722 --> 00:26:54.696
The next day, Klaus asked me to see a film with him again.

00:26:54.756 --> 00:26:57.539
But I told him I couldn't go.

00:26:57.600 --> 00:27:03.784
And when I met Janet for lunch, I told her about me and Tony.

00:27:03.844 --> 00:27:08.288
Everything's going very well, I said.

00:27:08.348 --> 00:27:11.794
Tony makes me very happy.

00:27:11.854 --> 00:27:14.450
She looked at me.

00:27:14.510 --> 00:27:18.494
Does he talk about Cathy when he's with you?

00:27:18.554 --> 00:27:20.385
She asked.

00:27:20.445 --> 00:27:25.720
He has to see Cathy because of Daisy, I told her.

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:27.862
But that's all.

00:27:27.922 --> 00:27:30.914
Good, Janet said.

00:27:30.974 --> 00:27:33.446
But she didn't smile.

00:27:33.506 --> 00:27:39.370
I looked at her It's okay, Janet, I said.

00:27:39.431 --> 00:27:41.992
Tony's a good man.

00:27:42.052 --> 00:27:44.774
He wants to be with me.

00:27:44.835 --> 00:27:48.566
Good, said Janet again.

00:27:48.626 --> 00:27:52.810
Because I only want you to be happy, Stella.

00:27:52.870 --> 00:27:55.450
And I was happy.

00:27:55.510 --> 00:27:57.609
for two months.

00:27:57.669 --> 00:28:00.360
I saw Tony every day.

00:28:00.421 --> 00:28:06.775
Sometimes Daisy was with us and sometimes it was just me and Tony.

00:28:06.835 --> 00:28:13.680
We went to see films, we walked in the park and I cooked meals for him.

00:28:13.740 --> 00:28:16.812
We talked and laughed a lot.

00:28:16.872 --> 00:28:21.484
Oh yes, I was very happy.

00:28:21.544 --> 00:28:28.981
And then one evening in October everything changed.

00:28:29.042 --> 00:28:34.786
I left work to walk home and I saw James in a bar.

00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:36.907
He was with a woman.

00:28:36.967 --> 00:28:41.330
They were laughing and they looked happy.

00:28:41.390 --> 00:28:48.306
He laughed with me like that when he was my boyfriend, I thought.

00:28:48.366 --> 00:28:52.728
And I wanted to go into the restaurant to talk to the woman.

00:28:52.788 --> 00:28:58.232
I wanted to say to her, James is no good.

00:28:58.292 --> 00:29:00.544
But I didn't.

00:29:00.604 --> 00:29:03.788
I just walked up the street.

00:29:03.848 --> 00:29:07.140
But I was sad for her.

00:29:07.201 --> 00:29:15.018
Then, when I got back to Bridge Street, I saw Tony in front of his house.

00:29:15.078 --> 00:29:17.750
He was with a woman too.

00:29:17.810 --> 00:29:20.594
A woman I didn't know.

00:29:20.654 --> 00:29:25.488
I saw Tony look down into the woman's face.

00:29:25.548 --> 00:29:30.250
He looks at me like that, I thought.

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:33.812
He stands near me like that.

00:29:33.872 --> 00:29:38.314
The woman's hair was black and very long.

00:29:38.374 --> 00:29:40.664
She was beautiful.

00:29:40.724 --> 00:29:45.486
She said something and put her hand on Tony's arm.

00:29:45.546 --> 00:29:49.168
Then I saw Tony walk to his front door.

00:29:49.228 --> 00:29:54.272
He looked back at the woman and said something to her.

00:29:54.332 --> 00:29:58.614
I knew he wanted her to go into the house with him.

00:29:58.674 --> 00:30:02.416
Don't go in, I thought.

00:30:02.476 --> 00:30:07.709
But she did go in and Tony closed the door.

00:30:07.769 --> 00:30:12.572
I went into my house and closed my door.

00:30:12.632 --> 00:30:17.435
I sat down and thought about James again.

00:30:17.495 --> 00:30:21.718
James always had lots of girlfriends.

00:30:21.778 --> 00:30:26.380
Does Tony want me and that woman?

00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:30.972
But I didn't know the answer.

00:30:31.032 --> 00:30:38.276
Chapter 5 Who is that woman?

00:30:38.336 --> 00:30:44.841
I didn't see Tony that evening and he didn't phone me.

00:30:44.901 --> 00:30:50.494
When I left for work the next day, his car wasn't there.

00:30:50.554 --> 00:30:53.926
Was he with that woman?

00:30:53.986 --> 00:30:56.557
Are you okay?

00:30:56.617 --> 00:31:00.428
Klaus asked me when I got to the restaurant.

00:31:00.488 --> 00:31:03.859
Yes, thank you, I said.

00:31:03.919 --> 00:31:08.761
I didn't want to talk to him about Tony and the woman.

00:31:08.821 --> 00:31:12.769
I didn't want to talk to anyone about them.

00:31:12.829 --> 00:31:17.668
But I thought about them a lot, all day.

00:31:17.729 --> 00:31:25.083
After work, I went quickly back to Bridge Street, but not to my house.

00:31:25.143 --> 00:31:28.064
I went to Tony's house.

00:31:28.125 --> 00:31:32.618
Hi, he said when he came to the door.

00:31:32.678 --> 00:31:37.160
He looked tired, and he didn't kiss me.

00:31:37.221 --> 00:31:38.937
Come in.

00:31:38.997 --> 00:31:41.634
We went into the living room.

00:31:41.694 --> 00:31:44.796
He had a cup of coffee on the table.

00:31:44.856 --> 00:31:47.906
Sorry, he said.

00:31:47.966 --> 00:31:50.478
Do you want something to drink?

00:31:50.538 --> 00:31:53.319
No, I said.

00:31:53.379 --> 00:31:57.861
I want to speak to you about yesterday.

00:31:57.881 --> 00:32:03.053
I saw you with a woman.

00:32:03.113 --> 00:32:05.654
Tony looked down.

00:32:05.714 --> 00:32:08.632
Oh, he said.

00:32:08.692 --> 00:32:12.022
I waited for him to speak.

00:32:12.082 --> 00:32:16.714
It isn't what you think, Stella, he said.

00:32:16.774 --> 00:32:19.176
I looked at him.

00:32:19.236 --> 00:32:24.010
Stella, that was Cathy, Tony said.

00:32:24.070 --> 00:32:26.150
I sat down.

00:32:26.210 --> 00:32:29.152
I didn't know what to say.

00:32:29.212 --> 00:32:31.914
She wanted to talk to me.

00:32:31.974 --> 00:32:33.895
About what?

00:32:33.956 --> 00:32:36.600
Tony didn't answer.

00:32:36.660 --> 00:32:40.364
I thought about the two of them in the street.

00:32:40.424 --> 00:32:44.026
Tony, I asked.

00:32:44.086 --> 00:32:47.648
Do you still love Cathy?

00:32:47.708 --> 00:32:50.340
He looked up at me.

00:32:50.400 --> 00:32:53.381
No, he said.

00:32:53.441 --> 00:32:55.972
Do you think that?

00:32:56.032 --> 00:33:00.236
I don't know what to think, I said.

00:33:00.296 --> 00:33:03.168
Tony took my hand.

00:33:03.228 --> 00:33:06.799
Oh, Stella, he said.

00:33:06.860 --> 00:33:10.942
Of course I don't still love Cathy.

00:33:11.002 --> 00:33:12.732
You don't?

00:33:12.792 --> 00:33:14.252
I asked.

00:33:14.312 --> 00:33:16.884
I looked into his eyes.

00:33:16.944 --> 00:33:21.186
James didn't like me to look into his eyes like that.

00:33:21.246 --> 00:33:24.587
But Tony looked back into my eyes.

00:33:24.647 --> 00:33:28.133
He didn't look away.

00:33:28.193 --> 00:33:33.430
I want to hate Cathy," he told me.

00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:35.182
But I can't.

00:33:35.242 --> 00:33:37.824
She's Daisy's mother.

00:33:37.884 --> 00:33:43.938
I know you think about the time when you were a family, I told him.

00:33:43.999 --> 00:33:47.072
You, Cathy, and Daisy.

00:33:47.132 --> 00:33:49.834
Yes, he said.

00:33:49.894 --> 00:33:52.396
I do think about that.

00:33:52.456 --> 00:33:56.128
I think about it because of Daisy.

00:33:56.188 --> 00:34:00.661
But I don't want to be with Cathy now, Stella.

00:34:00.721 --> 00:34:03.852
I want to be with you."

00:34:03.912 --> 00:34:07.243
Now I couldn't look at him.

00:34:07.303 --> 00:34:10.924
I felt small and afraid.

00:34:10.984 --> 00:34:12.364
Do you?

00:34:12.384 --> 00:34:14.725
I asked.

00:34:14.785 --> 00:34:17.816
Yes, he said.

00:34:17.876 --> 00:34:19.507
You know I do.

00:34:19.527 --> 00:34:22.297
I like you, Stella.

00:34:22.358 --> 00:34:24.428
I like you a lot.

00:34:24.488 --> 00:34:29.604
Actually, I looked up at him again.

00:34:29.664 --> 00:34:32.958
He smiled at me.

00:34:33.019 --> 00:34:37.699
Actually, I think I love you, Stella.

00:34:37.759 --> 00:34:42.090
No, I know I love you.

00:34:42.150 --> 00:34:44.961
I was happy again.

00:34:44.981 --> 00:34:52.122
Oh, Tony, I said, I love you too.

00:34:52.182 --> 00:34:57.834
Come here, he said, and he kissed me.

00:34:57.894 --> 00:35:02.808
But I knew there was still something wrong.

00:35:02.868 --> 00:35:11.672
Kathy came here yesterday because she wanted to tell me something, he said.

00:35:11.732 --> 00:35:16.176
She and Cameron want to live in Scotland.

00:35:16.236 --> 00:35:23.480
They want to buy a house there and they want to take Daisy with them.

00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:26.001
I looked at him.

00:35:26.061 --> 00:35:30.092
Oh, Tony, I said.

00:35:30.152 --> 00:35:32.702
She can't do that.

00:35:32.762 --> 00:35:35.914
Tony looked down again.

00:35:35.974 --> 00:35:39.774
I think she can, he said.

00:35:39.835 --> 00:35:44.396
She's Daisy's mother, and Daisy lives with her.

00:35:44.456 --> 00:35:51.748
Cameron has a new job in Scotland, and Kathy can get a job there as a teacher.

00:35:51.808 --> 00:35:57.173
But Daisy needs you too, I said.

00:35:57.233 --> 00:36:01.139
Tony couldn't answer for a minute.

00:36:01.199 --> 00:36:03.480
He was too sad.

00:36:03.540 --> 00:36:07.403
Then he tried to smile.

00:36:07.463 --> 00:36:12.796
I don't know what to do, Stella, he said.

00:36:12.856 --> 00:36:16.940
I just don't know what to do.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:21.102
We can speak to someone who can help us.

00:36:21.162 --> 00:36:23.794
A lawyer, I said.

00:36:23.854 --> 00:36:26.066
We can stop her.

00:36:26.126 --> 00:36:28.582
That's what we can do.

00:36:28.642 --> 00:36:31.408
Tony looked at me.

00:36:31.468 --> 00:36:37.192
We can try, he said.

00:36:37.252 --> 00:36:49.961
Chapter 6 A Family Again So we went to see a lawyer, a Mrs. Scott.

00:36:50.021 --> 00:36:54.734
I couldn't talk to Kathy's lawyer, she told us.

00:36:54.794 --> 00:37:07.588
And then we can go to the family court She looked at Tony, but I must tell you, Mr. Bryant, it isn't going to be easy.

00:37:07.649 --> 00:37:14.862
The family courts often think a child needs to be with his or her mother.

00:37:14.922 --> 00:37:21.755
Daisy needs her father too, I said, and Mrs. Scott smiled.

00:37:21.815 --> 00:37:24.416
Yes, she said.

00:37:24.476 --> 00:37:26.297
I know that.

00:37:26.357 --> 00:37:28.800
We can only try.

00:37:28.860 --> 00:37:31.974
Thank you, said Tony.

00:37:32.034 --> 00:37:34.275
Then we left.

00:37:34.336 --> 00:37:38.717
The next two days were not easy.

00:37:38.778 --> 00:37:45.881
Then Mrs. Scott phoned and said that the family court was next Tuesday.

00:37:45.941 --> 00:37:50.503
Daisy came to us the weekend before the family court.

00:37:50.563 --> 00:37:54.685
The weather was bad, so we watched TV.

00:37:54.745 --> 00:38:01.438
There was a film about horses on television Daisy looked up at us.

00:38:01.498 --> 00:38:06.400
Cameron says I can have a horse when we live in Scotland.

00:38:06.460 --> 00:38:07.991
She said.

00:38:08.052 --> 00:38:11.994
He wants to teach me all about horses.

00:38:12.054 --> 00:38:15.266
That's nice, Tony said.

00:38:15.326 --> 00:38:18.197
But I knew he was sad.

00:38:18.258 --> 00:38:20.729
I took his hand.

00:38:20.789 --> 00:38:26.082
But I want you to teach me about horses, Daddy.

00:38:26.142 --> 00:38:28.044
Daisy said.

00:38:28.104 --> 00:38:33.038
When he heard that, Tony smiled.

00:38:33.098 --> 00:38:36.149
Can you teach me, Daddy?

00:38:36.209 --> 00:38:38.220
Daisy asked.

00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:41.422
Tony gave her a kiss.

00:38:41.482 --> 00:38:45.534
Yes, baby, he said.

00:38:45.594 --> 00:38:52.408
But that evening, when Daisy was in bed, Tony looked at me.

00:38:52.468 --> 00:38:55.630
What do I know about horses?

00:38:55.690 --> 00:38:58.697
He said, nothing.

00:38:58.757 --> 00:39:02.374
I only know about computers.

00:39:02.434 --> 00:39:06.285
No, you don't, I said.

00:39:06.345 --> 00:39:09.606
You know how to love Daisy.

00:39:09.666 --> 00:39:12.696
And that's what's important.

00:39:12.756 --> 00:39:16.227
He kissed me and smiled.

00:39:16.287 --> 00:39:23.729
I'm very happy I came to live next door to you, Stella Greenwood, he said.

00:39:23.789 --> 00:39:28.283
On Tuesday, we went to the family court.

00:39:28.343 --> 00:39:32.257
Kathy was there with her lawyer and Cameron.

00:39:32.317 --> 00:39:36.178
Daisy was at home with Kathy's mother.

00:39:36.238 --> 00:39:39.308
Tony's hand was in mine.

00:39:39.368 --> 00:39:43.359
He didn't look over at Kathy or Cameron.

00:39:43.419 --> 00:39:46.870
Then the judge came into the court.

00:39:46.930 --> 00:39:51.062
He was a small man with grey hair.

00:39:51.122 --> 00:39:54.724
We were in the court for 30 minutes.

00:39:54.784 --> 00:40:00.606
Mrs. Scott spoke for Tony, and Kathy's lawyer spoke for Kathy.

00:40:00.666 --> 00:40:04.838
The judge listened, and he asked some questions.

00:40:04.898 --> 00:40:08.469
Mrs. Scott and Kathy's lawyer answered them.

00:40:08.529 --> 00:40:15.782
Then the judge looked at us, and he said what we didn't want him to say.

00:40:15.842 --> 00:40:19.626
I'm sorry, Mr. Bryant.

00:40:19.687 --> 00:40:22.701
I think that's all I heard him say.

00:40:22.721 --> 00:40:30.822
I just sat next to Tony and thought, no, no, no, no.

00:40:30.882 --> 00:40:34.794
Tony put his head in his hands.

00:40:34.854 --> 00:40:40.595
He didn't say anything, but I knew he was angry.

00:40:40.655 --> 00:40:47.786
When the judge and the lawyers left the court, Kathy came over to talk to Tony.

00:40:47.846 --> 00:40:51.009
But he didn't want to look at her.

00:40:51.070 --> 00:40:57.706
You can still see Daisy at any time, Tony, she told him.

00:40:57.766 --> 00:41:00.138
But he didn't answer.

00:41:00.198 --> 00:41:03.681
Then Cathy left with Cameron.

00:41:03.741 --> 00:41:07.364
I sat there next to Tony.

00:41:07.424 --> 00:41:11.016
I didn't know what to say to him.

00:41:11.076 --> 00:41:16.554
But then I thought about what Janet always said to me.

00:41:16.614 --> 00:41:21.342
When you want to do something, just do it.

00:41:21.402 --> 00:41:23.473
Don't stop and think.

00:41:23.533 --> 00:41:25.044
Don't wait.

00:41:25.104 --> 00:41:27.636
Just do it.

00:41:27.696 --> 00:41:31.878
And I knew what I wanted to do.

00:41:31.938 --> 00:41:37.202
Tony, I said, look at me.

00:41:37.262 --> 00:41:39.884
His face was white.

00:41:39.944 --> 00:41:44.438
I took his hands and looked into his eyes.

00:41:44.498 --> 00:41:47.830
Look, I said.

00:41:47.890 --> 00:41:54.513
There are computers in Scotland and lots of restaurants.

00:41:54.573 --> 00:41:57.064
What are you saying?

00:41:57.124 --> 00:41:58.864
He asked.

00:41:58.924 --> 00:42:01.024
I smiled.

00:42:01.084 --> 00:42:05.085
I'm saying we can live near Daisy.

00:42:05.145 --> 00:42:10.276
I'm saying we can go to Scotland.

00:42:10.336 --> 00:42:13.097
Tony smiled at me.

00:42:13.157 --> 00:42:15.888
A big smile.

00:42:15.948 --> 00:42:17.893
Me and you.

00:42:17.953 --> 00:42:27.100
He said, yes, I said, me, you and Daisy too.

00:42:27.160 --> 00:42:32.111
And in January, that's what we did.

00:42:32.171 --> 00:42:35.082
We went to live in Scotland.

00:42:35.142 --> 00:42:42.784
I got a job as a chef for a hotel and Tony got a good job with computers.

00:42:42.844 --> 00:42:44.748
And Daisy?

00:42:44.808 --> 00:42:49.029
Well, we see her every weekend.

00:42:49.089 --> 00:43:02.406
She's teaching Tony about horses.

00:43:02.466 --> 00:43:15.087
Here's the beginning of another book at this level.

00:43:15.148 --> 00:43:18.740
Bad Love by Sue Leather.

00:43:18.800 --> 00:43:23.183
I met Dr. Jack Daley in August.

00:43:23.243 --> 00:43:25.974
It was a Saturday afternoon.

00:43:26.034 --> 00:43:31.598
I was at a party in Denver at my friend Judy Kaplan's house.

00:43:31.658 --> 00:43:35.551
We were in the backyard and it was hot.

00:43:35.611 --> 00:43:39.284
It's always hot in the summer in Denver.

00:43:39.344 --> 00:43:41.974
It was a good party.

00:43:42.034 --> 00:43:48.246
About 50 people were there, and there were drinks and good food.

00:43:48.306 --> 00:43:52.888
I walked around the backyard and talked to people.

00:43:52.948 --> 00:43:56.309
I had a drink and tried some food.

00:43:56.369 --> 00:44:00.320
And then I met Jack Daley.

00:44:00.380 --> 00:44:02.822
Hi, he said.

00:44:02.882 --> 00:44:06.293
He had black hair and blue eyes.

00:44:06.353 --> 00:44:08.094
My name's Jack.

00:44:08.154 --> 00:44:09.854
Jack Daley.

00:44:09.914 --> 00:44:12.052
Hi, I said.

00:44:12.112 --> 00:44:13.490
I'm Flick.

00:44:13.551 --> 00:44:15.152
Flick Lane.

00:44:15.212 --> 00:44:17.172
We talked a little.

00:44:17.232 --> 00:44:24.926
He told me he was a doctor, and that he worked at the University of Colorado Hospital in Denver.

00:44:24.986 --> 00:44:26.628
What about you?

00:44:26.688 --> 00:44:28.178
He asked me.

00:44:28.238 --> 00:44:30.740
I'm a detective, I said.

00:44:30.800 --> 00:44:33.332
Denver Police Department.

00:44:33.392 --> 00:44:35.362
Oh, a cop.

00:44:35.422 --> 00:44:37.234
He said with a smile.

00:44:37.294 --> 00:44:40.225
He had very white teeth.

00:44:40.285 --> 00:44:42.666
I smiled back at him.

00:44:42.726 --> 00:44:45.886
Yeah, I said, a cop.

00:44:45.946 --> 00:44:48.278
So where's your police car?

00:44:48.338 --> 00:44:52.080
He said, that's my car over there.

00:44:52.140 --> 00:44:59.924
I said, it's the red 1957 Chevrolet, a 57 Chevy.

00:44:59.984 --> 00:45:02.275
That's a beautiful car.

00:45:02.335 --> 00:45:06.256
He said, I love old Chevys.

00:45:06.316 --> 00:45:09.558
We talked some more about cars.

00:45:09.618 --> 00:45:15.622
Then Okay, he said, now tell me more about you.

00:45:15.682 --> 00:45:21.728
Well, I said, my first name's Felicity.

00:45:21.788 --> 00:45:23.230
I laughed.

00:45:23.290 --> 00:45:24.962
Felicity.

00:45:25.022 --> 00:45:31.458
Yes, I said, my dad liked it, but please call me Flick.

00:45:31.518 --> 00:45:34.060
We talked a little more.

00:45:34.120 --> 00:45:39.240
After some minutes he said, Well, I'm leaving now, Flick.

00:45:39.300 --> 00:45:42.020
Can I see you again sometime?"

00:45:42.080 --> 00:45:44.101
He smiled again.

00:45:44.161 --> 00:45:46.982
He had a beautiful smile.

00:45:47.042 --> 00:45:49.332
I smiled too.

00:45:49.392 --> 00:45:54.554
Okay, sure, I said, and gave him my phone number.

00:45:54.614 --> 00:45:59.695
He walked slowly out of the backyard, and I watched him.

00:45:59.755 --> 00:46:01.566
Tall and dark.

00:46:01.626 --> 00:46:04.096
Nice, I thought.

00:46:04.156 --> 00:46:09.736
Later, after the party, I talked to Judy about Daley.

00:46:09.796 --> 00:46:13.338
Tell me about the doctor, I said.

00:46:13.398 --> 00:46:15.199
Jack Daley?

00:46:15.260 --> 00:46:17.251
Judy looked at me.

00:46:17.311 --> 00:46:19.812
He's a very good doctor.

00:46:19.872 --> 00:46:22.294
All the rich people go to him.

00:46:22.355 --> 00:46:25.908
You know, movie stars, sports stars.

00:46:25.968 --> 00:46:28.590
He's famous at the hospital.

00:46:28.650 --> 00:46:33.458
Judy is a doctor too, at the university hospital.

00:46:33.518 --> 00:46:36.495
Oh, famous is he, I said.

00:46:36.515 --> 00:46:40.106
I don't often like famous people.

00:46:40.166 --> 00:46:43.047
Judy looked into my eyes.

00:46:43.107 --> 00:46:47.238
Oh, come on, Detective Lane, she said.

00:46:47.298 --> 00:46:48.778
You like him.

00:46:48.798 --> 00:46:51.710
I watched you with him.

00:46:51.770 --> 00:46:53.660
All the women like him.

